bleiben:
{{also|Bleiben}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|beleiben||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|blīben}}, {{m|gmh|belīben||to remain in the same position, pause, blin}}, from {{inh|de|goh|bilīban||to remain}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*bilībaną||to remain}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*leyp-||to stick, glue}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|blijven||to remain}}, {{cog|en|belive||to remain, stay}}. More at {{m|en|belive}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈblaɪ̯bən/|[ˈblaɪ̯bən]|[ˈblaɪ̯bm̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-bleiben.ogg|a=Germany}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-bleiben.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{audio|de|De-bleiben3.ogg|a=<<Germany>> (<<Berlin>>)}}
* {{audio|de|De-bleiben2.ogg|a=<<Germany>> (<<Berlin>>)}}
* {{hyphenation|de|blei|ben}}
* {{rhyme|de|aɪ̯bən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|bleiben<blieb,geblieben.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|copulative|with a predicate adjective or predicate nominative}} to [[remain]] {{gloss|to continue to be}}
#: {{ux|de|Er '''blieb''' sein ganzes Leben ein glühender Anhänger der Monarchie.|He '''remained''' a devoted supporter of the monarchy for all his life.}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1929|author=w:Kurt Tucholsky|title=s:de:Das Lächeln der Mona Lisa (Sammelband)|publisher=w:Rowohlt Verlag|page=239
|passage=Um populär zu werden, kann man seine eigene Meinung behalten. Um populär zu '''bleiben''', weniger.|t=In order to become popular, one can keep one’s own opinion. In order to '''stay''' popular, less so.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[keep]] (on); to [[continue]] {{+obj|de|inf<doing something>}} {{q|see usage notes below}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''bleibe''' noch ein bisschen liegen.|I'll '''keep''' lying here for a bit.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[stay]]; to [[remain]] in a place
#: {{ux|de|Du kannst ja schon fahren, aber ich '''bleibe''' noch.|Feel free to leave, but I'm '''staying''' some more.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[be]]; to be [[stuck]] {{q|implying tardiness}}
#: {{ux|de|Wo '''bleibst''' du? Wir sind schon seit über einer Stunde da.|Where '''are''' you? We arrived more than an hour ago.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to be [[left]] {{+obj|de|dat<for someone>}}
#: {{ux|de|Was '''bleibt''' ihm jetzt noch, wo seine Frau gestorben ist?|What does he have '''left''' now that his wife is dead?|lit=What is left for him...}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[stick]], to [[stay]] {{+obj|de|:bei(dat)<with something, e.g. an opinion>}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich hab’s ihm erklärt, aber er '''bleibt''' bei seiner Meinung.|I’ve explained it to him, but he '''sticks''' with his opinion.}}
# {{lb|de|auxiliary}} to [[remain]] {{+obj|de|:zu(active&inf)<to be done>}}
#: {{ux|de|Es '''bleibt abzuwarten''', ob sich der Erfolg einstellt.|It '''remains to be seen''' whether success will be achieved.)}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|keep on}} The construction ''bleiben'' + infinitive is only possible with certain verbs that describe a fixed position. These are foremost {{m|de|stehen||to stand}}, {{m|de|sitzen||to sit}}, {{m|de|liegen||to lie}}, and synonyms of them. It is also common with verbs like {{m|de|hängen|t=to hang}}, {{m|de|kleben|t=to stick}}, {{m|de|stecken|t=to be jammed}}. Chiefly informally, it may be used with certain verbs describing a continuous living situation, e.g. {{m|de|leben||to live}}, {{m|de|wohnen||to dwell}}, or {{m|de|arbeiten||to work, be employed}}.

