===Verb===
{{de-verb|geben<gibt#gab,gegeben,gäbe>}}

# {{lb|de|ditransitive}} to [[give]] {{q|changing ownership}} {{+obj|de|dat<someone> + acc<something>}}
#: {{syn|de|schenken}}
#: {{uxi|de|Meine Frau hat mir eine neue Uhr '''gegeben'''.|My wife '''gave''' me a new watch.}}
# {{lb|de|ditransitive}} to [[hand]], to [[pass]], to put within reach {{+obj|de|dat<someone> + acc<something>}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Gib''' mir das!|'''Give''' me that!}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Gib''' mir deine Hand.|'''Give''' me your hand (to hold).}}
#: {{uxi|de|Könnten Sie mir den Stift '''geben'''?|Could you '''hand''' me that pen?}}
# {{lb|de|impersonal|transitive}} {{ng|Used to indicate that something exists (often with a certain property and/or in a certain location). Usually translated as {{m|en|there be|there is/are}} or {{m|en|there exist|there exist(s)}}}} {{+obj|de|acc}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Gibt''' es gute Schulen in der Nähe?|'''Are''' there good schools in the neighborhood?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Es '''gibt''' kein Wasser in dieser Wüste.|There '''is''' no water in this desert.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das kann es nicht '''geben'''.|This is nothing that could possibly '''exist'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=2000|title=Eurobarometer: Public Opinion in the European Union|isbn=075671320X|page=8|text=Es '''gibt''' eine europäische kulturelle Identität, die von allen Europäern geteilt wird.|t=There '''is''' a European cultural identity, which is shared by all Europeans.}}
## {{ng|Used to indicate that something is on offer or being handed out, e.g. food for a meal or items sold in a shop}}
##: {{uxi|de|Was '''gibt''' es heute zum Mittag?|What''''s''' for lunch today?}}
##: {{uxi|de|Da hinten '''gibt''' es leckeres Eis.|'''They have''' tasty ice cream (on offer) over there.}}
# {{lb|de|ditransitive|transitive}} to [[communicate]] {{q|helpful information such as a hint or advice}}, to [[signal]] {{q|in a certain way such as a sign}}
#: {{uxi|de|Darf ich dir einen Rat '''geben'''?|May I '''give''' you some advice?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Der Spieler '''gab''' ein Signal, dass er eingewechselt werden wollte.|The player '''gave''' a signal that he wanted to be substituted.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[present]]; to [[put]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[result in]]
#: {{syn|de|ergeben}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|often|impersonal}} to [[stop]], to [[pass]], to [[sort out|sort itself out]] {{q|of difficulties, problems, pain, etc.}}
